Installation and Configuration of Google App Engine (Python)
1. Prerequisites
A Google account
Python 3.7 or later installed

pip package manager
Admin access to your computer
Google Cloud SDK


2. Create a Google Cloud Project
Go to: https://console.cloud.google.com
Click “Create Project”
Enter a project name and click “Create”
Note your Project ID


3. Install Google Cloud SDK
Visit: https://cloud.google.com/sdk/docs/install
Download and install the SDK for your OS
Open a terminal or command prompt and run:

gcloud init
Login to your Google account and select your project

4. Install App Engine Python Component
Run the following command in terminal:

gcloud components install app-engine-python

5. Create a Simple Python Web App for App Engine
a. Create a folder for your app:

mkdir myapp
cd myapp

b. Create a file named main.py:

from flask import Flask
app = Flask(__name__)
@app.route('/')
def hello():
    return 'Hello, Google App Engine!'

if __name__ == '__main__':
    app.run()

c. Create a file named- requirements.txt:
flask

d. Create a file named app.yaml:

runtime: python39
handlers:
  - url: /.*
    script: auto

6. Deploy to Google App Engine
Make sure you're inside the app folder (myapp) and run:
gcloud app deploy
Confirm when prompted. After deployment, open your app in a browser:
gcloud app browse

7. Output
Your app will be live at:
https://<your-project-id>.appspot.com
It should display:

"Hello, Google App Engine!"
